  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "The writer Whitley Strieber, on Jesse Michels' podcast, passes on what he says an Air Force general named Arthur Exon told him. According to Strieber, when wreckage and bodies from a 1947 crash near Roswell, New Mexico, were brought to the military's equipment command at Wright Field, Exon held one of the bodies himself, and it felt like a big insect. If true, it would mean the military recovered non-human bodies in 1947."
